      "agent_response": {
        "response": "[Awaiting tool approval]\n\n**Policy:** Shell command approval (skills demo)\nAbout to run a shell command in the agent workspace. Approve to continue?\n**Required Tools:** run_command\n```python\ninstall_out = await run_command(\"uv pip install openpyxl python-docx PyPDF2 pdf2docx PyMuPDF Pillow pytesseract icalendar fire litellm\")\nprint(install_out[:200])\n\nverify = await run_command(\"python -c \\\"import openpyxl; print('ok')\\\"\")\nprint(verify)\n\nsearch_result = await run_command(\"python3 skills/OfficeBench/tools/shell/command.py --command 'find /workspace -name \\\"order_summary.xlsx\\\" 2>/dev/null'\")\nprint(search_result)\n\n# Also try a broader search and check testbed structure\nsearch2 = await search_files(\".\", \"**/*order_summary*\")\nprint(search2)\n\n# Check testbed directory structure\ntestbed_files = await list_files(\"./testbed\")\nprint(testbed_files)\n\n# Check testbed/data if it exists\ntestbed_data = await list_files(\"./testbed/data\")\nprint(testbed_data)\n\n# Read the Excel file using the OfficeBench tool with the correct testbed path\nexcel_output = await run_command(\"python3 skills/OfficeBench/tools/excel/read_file.py --file_path /workspace/testbed/data/order_summary.xlsx\")\nprint(excel_output)\n\n# Parse the output to find the order ORD-6C71B1\nlines = excel_output.strip().split('\\n')\n# Find all lines containing ORD-6C71B1\norder_lines = [l for l in lines if 'ORD-6C71B1' in l]\n# Also get the header row (row 1)\nheader_lines = [l for l in lines if l.startswith('(1,')]\nprint(\"=== Headers ===\")\nfor h in header_lines:\n    print(h)\nprint(\"\\n=== Order ORD-6C71B1 data ===\")\nfor ol in order_lines:\n    print(ol)\n\n# Let me get all cells to understand the structure better\n# Headers are in row 1, let me find which row has ORD-6C71B1\nimport re\n\ncells = {}\nfor line in lines:\n    match = re.match(r'\\((\\d+),\\s*(\\d+)\\):\\s*(.*)', line.strip())\n    if match:\n        row, col, val = int(match.group(1)), int(match.group(2)), match.group(3).strip()\n        cells[(row, col)] = val\n\n# Get headers (row 1)\nmax_col = max(c for (r, c) in cells.keys())\nheaders = {col: cells.get((1, col), '') for col in range(1, max_col + 1)}\n\n# Find the row with ORD-6C71B1\norder_row = None\nfor (r, c), v in cells.items():\n    if v == 'ORD-6C71B1':\n        order_row = r\n        break\n\nif order_row:\n    print(f\"Order ORD-6C71B1 found in row {order_row}\\n\")\n    print(\"=== Order ORD-6C71B1 Summary ===\")\n    for col in range(1, max_col + 1):\n        header = headers.get(col, f'Col{col}')\n        value = cells.get((order_row, col), 'N/A')\n        print(f\"  {header}: {value}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Order ORD-6C71B1 not found in the spreadsheet\")\n```",
