      "agent_response": {
        "response": "[Awaiting tool approval]\n\n**Policy:** Shell command approval (skills demo)\nAbout to run a shell command in the agent workspace. Approve to continue?\n**Required Tools:** run_command\n```python\ninstall_out = await run_command(\"uv pip install openpyxl python-docx PyPDF2 pdf2docx PyMuPDF Pillow pytesseract icalendar fire litellm\")\nprint(\"Install done\")\n\nverify_out = await run_command(\"python -c \\\"import openpyxl; print('ok')\\\"\")\nprint(verify_out)\n\nfind_result = await run_command(\"python3 skills/OfficeBench/tools/shell/command.py --command 'find /workspace -name \\\"order_summary.xlsx\\\" 2>/dev/null'\")\nprint(find_result)\n\n# Also search via search_files\nsearch_result = await search_files(\".\", \"**/*order_summary*\")\nprint(search_result)\n\n# Let's check what's in the testbed directory\ntestbed_listing = await list_files(\"./testbed\")\nprint(testbed_listing)\n\n# Check testbed/data\ntestbed_data_listing = await list_files(\"./testbed/data\")\nprint(testbed_data_listing)\n\n# Now read the Excel file using the OfficeBench skill tool\nexcel_raw = await run_command(\"python3 skills/OfficeBench/tools/excel/read_file.py --file_path /workspace/testbed/data/order_summary.xlsx\")\nprint(excel_raw[:3000])\n\nparse_script = \"\"\"\nimport re, sys\n\nraw = open('/tmp/excel_output.txt').read()\nlines = raw.strip().split('\\\\n')\n\ncells = {}\nfor line in lines:\n    m = re.match(r'\\\\((\\\\d+),\\\\s*(\\\\d+)\\\\):\\\\s*(.*)', line.strip())\n    if m:\n        row, col, val = int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2)), m.group(3).strip()\n        if row not in cells:\n            cells[row] = {}\n        cells[row][col] = val\n\n# Get headers from row 1\nif 1 not in cells:\n    print(\"No header row found\")\n    sys.exit(1)\n\nheaders = cells[1]\nmax_col = max(headers.keys())\n\nprint(\"=== Column Headers ===\")\nfor c in range(1, max_col + 1):\n    print(f\"  Col {c}: {headers.get(c, '(empty)')}\")\n\n# Find the row containing ORD-6C71B1\norder_row = None\nfor r in cells:\n    for c in cells[r]:\n        if cells[r][c] == 'ORD-6C71B1':\n            order_row = r\n            break\n    if order_row:\n        break\n\nif order_row:\n    print(f\"\\\\n=== Order ORD-6C71B1 (Row {order_row}) ===\")\n    for c in range(1, max_col + 1):\n        h = headers.get(c, f'Col{c}')\n        v = cells.get(order_row, {}).get(c, 'N/A')\n        print(f\"  {h}: {v}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"\\\\nOrder ORD-6C71B1 not found in the spreadsheet.\")\n    print(\"All order IDs found:\")\n    for r in sorted(cells.keys()):\n        if r == 1:\n            continue\n        for c in cells[r]:\n            if 'ORD-' in str(cells[r][c]):\n                print(f\"  Row {r}: {cells[r][c]}\")\n\"\"\"\nawait write_file(\"./parse_order.py\", parse_script)\nprint(\"Script written\")\n\n# First save the excel output to a temp file, then run the parser\nsave_cmd = await run_command(\"python3 skills/OfficeBench/tools/excel/read_file.py --file_path /workspace/testbed/data/order_summary.xlsx > /tmp/excel_output.txt\")\nprint(\"Saved excel output to temp file\")\n\nparse_result = await run_command(\"python ./parse_order.py\")\nprint(parse_result)\n```",
